</pre> pp.plot(t); <p>Besides the standard formatting options available in <code>pathpyG</code>, temporal plots come with specific options tailored to their unique nature. These specialized settings allow for precise control over the time dimension of the visualization. The <code>delta</code> option lets you adjust the progression speed through the time steps of your visualization. Here, a value of 1000 translates to a one-second interval, providing a way to calibrate the pace at which the temporal data unfolds.</p> In [ ]: Copied! <pre>color = {"a": "blue", "b": "red", "c": "green", "d": "yellow"}
pp.plot(t, node_color=color, delta=2500);
